From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:04:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] presentation: panorama placeholders follow the shelf and
 placed cells keep their slot
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Browse source panorama laid unknown covers out as WIDE_COVER_RATIO 9/16.
That is under the 0.75 switch, so each cell was a wide 3:2 band spanning
two lanes. Most manga covers are tall, about 1.5 height/width, and nearly
every cell then flipped to a single lane. Since cross-band first commits
wait for settle, and header prefetch pauses while scrolling, those flips
all landed about 300 ms after each fling stopped. Each one was a full
structural relayout: content height 14098 to 4092 for 20 items and 31008
to 16957 for 59 items, with the anchor jumping 394-1628 px. The shelf
showed a wide block first, then shrank and reshuffled after every stop.

Unknown ids now use a process-wide placeholder, tall 3/2 by default, so
the slot and the drawn cover start as a book. committedRatio reports that
placeholder. The column vote still reads committedRatioOrNull and skips
unknowns, so the placeholder cannot vote for itself. When the grid
settles, onGridSignal sets the placeholder from the vote: Tall or Wide
forces that band; Unknown with at least one committed ratio follows the
majority, entering wide at 0.60 and leaving it at 0.40; a shelf with
nothing committed leaves the placeholder alone. A band flip clears frozen
slots and bumps the content epoch once, which is how a wide-thumb shelf
converges. The same band does not bump.

A first commit is compared with that placeholder, not with 9/16. The same
band commits immediately, including while scrolling, and does not bump.
A cross-band change stores the ratio either way and does not rebuild from
index 0. The masonry caches the band it queried on the rectangle. An id
placed strictly below the last visible index relayouts only the tail from
that index; rectangles above it are the same instances, and the change is
not structural, so the anchor is not restored. An id on screen or above
keeps the band already on its rectangle for this layout session.
committedRatio and rememberCoverRatio report that frozen band, so the
cover drawn with crop stays inside the slot it was given. The true ratio
is what the next layout session and the shape file use. Leaving the grid
drops freezes for keys no other grid still has placed.

The settle flush no longer commits every pending cross-band cover. It
still publishes the shape version so the placeholder sample can run.
Header prefetch no longer pauses while scrolling. The window is the first
visible row through the last visible row plus 60, with at most four
requests in flight. Cancel-behind, the finished set, and one retry stay.

A library shelf whose ratios are already committed lays out as before.
A tall file load matches the tall placeholder, so it no longer bumps the
content epoch.

